{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-1","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · dsh-synthv-studio：**A DSH plugin that finds a local Synthesizer V Studio 2 Pro, drives it through\nits own Lua scripting API, and gives the agent five tools for discovery, a\npersistent bridge, vocal composition, note editing and DAW integration.**\n\n[中文](README.zh.md) | English\n\n[](https://github.com/Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n[](LICENSE)\n[](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)\n[](#requirements)\n[](#requirements)","source":"extracted","section":"dsh-synthv-studio"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-2","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · dsh-synthv-studio：Synthesizer V Studio 2 Pro has no external API: it exposes **in-app Lua\nscripts** and a **VST3/ARA plug-in**. This plugin turns the script API into\nagent-callable tools by combining a persistent Lua executor, file-based IPC and a\nbundled local MCP server. It never parses or rewrites `.svp` project files, never\nopens a network port and never calls an online service — Synthesizer V remains\nthe only authority for project state.","source":"extracted","section":"dsh-synthv-studio"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-3","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · Requirements：- **Windows 10/11** (developed and verified on Windows 11; discovery and DAW\n  probing are Windows-specific).\n- **Synthesizer V Studio 2 Pro 2.1.2 or newer**, installed normally, with a\n  project open. Verified with 2.2.1.\n- **DeepSeek Harness with `dsh` ≥ 0.2.0-rc.1** (verified on the 0.2.0-rc.2\n  runtime shipped with DSH Desktop Next 2.0.17-next).\n- Node.js 20+ available to the DSH Host (the bundled bridge server is a plain\n  Node script).\n- Optionally any VST3 host (REAPER, Zrythm, Cubase, Studio One, …) for DAW work.","source":"extracted","section":"Requirements"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-4","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · Install：Install the bundle into a DSH profile:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile desktop add github:Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio\n```\n\n(or `--profile web` for the web profile). Restart DSH once after installing so\nthe Host plugin loads; the bundle is then listed under Settings → Plugins and the\nfive tools appear in new sessions.\n\n> An npm package is planned. The `dsh` install command will become\n> `dsh plugin add dsh-synthv-studio` once it is published; the GitHub install\n> above works today.","source":"extracted","section":"Install"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-5","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · First connection (once per SynthV launch)：1. In DSH, call `synthv_bridge` with `{ \"action\": \"ensure\" }`. On first use the\n   plugin writes the bridge scripts into\n   `%APPDATA%\\Dreamtonics\\Synthesizer V Studio 2\\scripts\\SynthV Agent Bridge\\`.\n2. In Synthesizer V, choose **Scripts → Rescan** once, then\n   **Scripts → SynthV Agent Bridge → Start SynthV Agent Bridge** and leave it\n   running.\n3. Call `synthv_bridge` with `{ \"action\": \"ensure\", \"waitSeconds\": 30 }` again.\n   A healthy bridge reports `connected`, a fresh heartbeat, and\n   `coherence.state = \"matched\"`.","source":"extracted","section":"First connection (once per SynthV launch)"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-6","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · First connection (once per SynthV launch)：The bridge is a SynthV script, so it stops with SynthV and must be started again\nafter the next launch. If a previously installed bridge was built from an older\ntemplate, `ensure` hot-reloads it instead of asking you to restart.","source":"extracted","section":"First connection (once per SynthV launch)"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-7","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · Tools：| Tool | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `synthv_detect` | Read-only scan: install directory and version, license session, voice database, VST3 + ARA bundles, installed DAWs, bridge heartbeat and IPC directory. |\n| `synthv_bridge` | `status` / `install` / `ensure` / `launch` / `stop` / `reload` / `uninstall`: installs the bundled Lua scripts, repairs a stale running bridge by hot reload, checks build coherence, starts Synthesizer V. |\n| `synthv_compose` | Writes a vocal phrase: tempo, track name, notes with lyrics, dedicated or reused note group, then an independent read-back check. `dryRun` plans without writing. |\n| `synthv_do` | Calls the bridge's own MCP tools: `sv_status`, `sv_describe`, `sv_query`, `sv_command`, `sv_ui`, `sv_review`. The bridge exposes 17 read actions, 38 write actions and 9 UI actions over notes, lyrics, phonemes, pitch controls, automation, voices/vocal modes, mixer and playback. |\n| `synthv_daw` | `detect` / `verify` / `export_midi` / `write_guide`: DAW detection, VST3/ARA verification, DAW plugin-cache evidence, Standard MIDI File export and a generated integration guide. |","source":"extracted","section":"Tools"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-8","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · Tools：Notes for `synthv_compose`: `onset` and `duration` are in **quarter-note beats**,\n`pitch` is a **MIDI note number**, `lyric` is one syllable.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"tempoBpm\": 104,\n  \"trackName\": \"Lead Vocal\",\n  \"groupName\": \"Lead Vocal\",\n\nFor advanced editing, call `synthv_do` with `sv_describe` first to read the exact\naction schema, then `sv_query` with `contextMode: \"writeIntent\"` to obtain a\n`contextId`, then `sv_command`. Every write is verified against SynthV's current\nstate by the bridge.","source":"extracted","section":"Tools"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-9","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · How it works：```text\nDSH agent\n   │  five synthv_* tools\n   ▼\ndsh-synthv-studio (Host plugin, lib/)\n\nThe Lua executor and the Node server share a content-derived build id\n(`sv3-lua-<version>-<sha256(template)>`). The plugin injects it at install time\nand writes the install manifest the executor uses to locate itself for hot\nreload, so the two halves can never disagree silently.","source":"extracted","section":"How it works"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-10","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · DAW integration：Synthesizer V Studio 2 Pro ships a **VST3 instrument plug-in** and a **VST3 ARA\nplug-in**. Typical workflow:","source":"extracted","section":"DAW integration"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-11","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · DAW integration：1. Insert `Synthesizer V Studio 2 Plugin` on an instrument track in your DAW.\n2. Export a melody with `synthv_daw { \"action\": \"export_midi\", \"bpm\": 104, \"notes\": [...] }`\n   and drag the `.mid` onto that track, or draw MIDI in the DAW.\n3. Write lyrics and tuning in the plug-in (or compose in the desktop app with\n   `synthv_compose` and save the project).\n4. Render/export from the DAW; the vocal follows the arrangement.\n5. Need a finished audio file? Render from the Synthesizer V desktop app and\n   import the WAV.","source":"extracted","section":"DAW integration"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-12","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · DAW integration：`synthv_daw { \"action\": \"write_guide\" }` writes a machine-specific Markdown guide\nwith the detected plug-in paths and DAW steps.","source":"extracted","section":"DAW integration"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-13","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · Limitations：- **Voice selection is manual.** The scripting API can neither read the current\n  singer nor enumerate installed singers, so you must pick one for the note group\n  in Synthesizer V's Voice panel before listening.\n- **Save and render stay in the GUI.** The official API cannot save the project\n  or render audio; `.svp` files are never touched by this plugin.\n- **The bridge lives inside SynthV.** It stops when SynthV closes and has to be\n  started from the Scripts menu after the next launch.\n- **Windows only.** macOS/Linux paths, process checks and DAW discovery are not\n  implemented.\n- One `synthv_compose` call targets one track. For multi-track work, create\n  tracks with `synthv_do` (`sv_command`, action `add_track`) and address them via\n  `trackIndex`.","source":"extracted","section":"Limitations"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-14","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · Tests：```sh\nnode test/selftest.mjs          # offline: plugin surface, schemas, pure logic\nnode test/mcp-handshake.mjs     # offline: bundled server MCP handshake\nnode test/e2e-synthv.mjs        # needs SynthV + bridge; dry run by default\nnode test/e2e-synthv.mjs --write\n\nReal-machine results are recorded in [docs/verification.md](docs/verification.md).","source":"extracted","section":"Tests"}
{"unit_id":"Making-acid__dsh-synthv-studio#readme-15","repo":"Making-acid/dsh-synthv-studio","commit":"c0443fff65c518d1b66f752a469ae9778e62690f","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-synthv-studio README · License and credits：Apache-2.0. The bundled bridge server (`server/server.bundle.mjs`) and the\nin-app Lua scripts (`synthv/*.lua`) are vendored from\n[SynthVCopilot/synthv-agent-bridge](https://github.com/SynthVCopilot/synthv-agent-bridge)\n(Apache-2.0) — see [NOTICE](NOTICE) for provenance and the build-id injection this\nplugin performs. “Synthesizer V” is a product of Dreamtonics Co., Ltd.; this\nproject is not affiliated with Dreamtonics.","source":"extracted","section":"License and credits"}
